A||||10||Doni Hagan||An un-stretched Lambo replica?||||5||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||10-16-2001||08:10 PM||||In this month's KIT CAR ILLUSTRATED or KIT CAR Magazine, there's an article on a car meet with a picture of what they say is a Lambo Countach replica built on an unstretched Fiero chassis. They added that the chassis had been steel reinforced but not enlongated. <P>According to the story, EURO-WORKS makes the replica. Has anyone heard about it and, if so, do you have any particulars about the kit?<P>I've e-mailed EURO-WORKS about the article and the car but haven't gotten any response from them. <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||RedRavenGT||10-16-2001||08:17 PM||||IFG makes one as well. If you go to their website I believe you can request literature in the mail. Thats what I did.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||10-16-2001||08:26 PM||||Thanks. I'll check it out immediately!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Juiced_V8||10-16-2001||08:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Doni Hagan:<BR><B>Thanks. I'll check it out immediately!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>mac s autobody aslo has unstretched lambos check him out<P><P>------------------<BR>86 gt v8 nos fogger<BR>cant find it-cant afford it? make it yourself||||reg||3
Z||000004||pherder||10-16-2001||09:07 PM||||The lastest, greatest thing is the <B>unstretched</B> frame <B><FONT SIZE="3">DIABLO!!!</FONT></B><P>Only Euro-Works has it (at this time.)<P>It is <B>STILL</B> a lot of work to put together.<P>The Artero (by PISA) is a Diablo look-a-like that fits an uncut Fiero frame.<P>Check out the Mall for one for sale.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FLASHY||10-16-2001||10:24 PM||||Yes there are a few companies that make un-stretched kits.<P><B>Mac's Autobody:</B> Retired, no longer in business. But here's the link anyway. <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/~macsautobody/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/~macsautobody/index.html</A> <P><B>EuroWorks Ltd:</B> The Mirage K is the un-stretched countach. The Mirage X is the un-stretched diablo. <A HREF="http://www.euroworksltd.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euroworksltd.com/</A> <P><B>I.F.G:</B> I think the 5000s model is an un-stretched but not definite.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ifgonline.com/ifg__replicas.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ifgonline.com/ifg__replicas.htm</A> <P><B>Lamboshop</B> They say they use un-stretched kits for ease, safety, and to avoid certain insurance hassles. <A HREF="http://www.lamboshop.com/frames2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lamboshop.com/frames2.htm</A> <P>Not sure of any other companies that have the un-stretched versions. Hope that helps!<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by FLASHY (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gerald||10-16-2001||10:50 PM||||LEAR 2000 makes a unstrecthed lambo conversion.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000007||FLASHY||10-16-2001||11:01 PM||||Oh ya! How could I have forgotten that one? It's even bookmarked on my computer. DUH*<P><B>Lear 2000:</B> They make the un-stretched diablo kit. I think it's the identical one to the Mirage X from EuroWorks. Cool site too! <A HREF="http://www.lear2000.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lear2000.com/</A> <P>Gerald: Have you been to their factory before? I'd love to go there and see it sometime. It's the only kitcar company close enough to my house. They don't sell the kits do they? Just the turnkeys I thought.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by FLASHY (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jason Kalbfleisch||10-16-2001||11:13 PM||||What they mean by steel reinforcement is that after the roof is cut off you must get strength back by welding box tube in the rockers and trianglulating back to pick up the upper frame rail or like IFG did,use an X brace under the car ||||reg||1
